## Input Format

Provided jobs mode:

```json
{
  "user_profile": {
    "skills": ["Python", "FastAPI", "Machine Learning"],
    "experience_years": 3,
    "desired_role": "Machine Learning Engineer",
    "preferences": {
      "location": "Remote"
    }
  },
  "job_listings": [
    {
      "job_title": "Machine Learning Engineer",
      "company": "Example AI",
      "job_description": "Build ML services using Python and APIs.",
      "required_skills": ["Python", "Machine Learning", "FastAPI"],
      "experience_level": "Mid",
      "location": "Remote",
      "apply_url": "https://example.com/apply",
      "source_platform": "Provided Dataset"
    }
  ]
}
```

Live jobs mode can omit `job_listings`.

## Output Format

The CLI prints strict JSON:

```json
{
  "user_profile_summary": {
    "target_role": "Machine Learning Engineer",
    "skills": ["Python", "FastAPI", "Machine Learning"],
    "experience_level": "Mid",
    "domain": "AI / Machine Learning"
  },
  "recommended_jobs": []
}
```

## Notes

- The project does not scrape LinkedIn or Indeed directly.
- Live results depend on the configured API provider and the apply sources it returns.
- Jobs with match scores below `50` are filtered out when there are enough listings to rank meaningfully.
- Ranking tie-breakers prioritize skills match, then role relevance.
